Key Takeaway

Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 application delivery service designed specifically for web applications. By providing intelligent routing, SSL termination, health monitoring, and Web Application Firewall protection, Application Gateway enables Azure Administrators to build secure, scalable, and highly available web application architectures. Understanding the differences between Application Gateway and Azure Load Balancer is essential for both the AZ-104 exam and real-world Azure deployments.
